Thought: The SMILES string "CC1=CC(=CC(=C1C2C=CC=CC=C2)C)O" is valid. This structure features a phenol group and a biphenyl moiety, which could match the NMR data with aromatic protons and a hydroxyl group. I will now check if this structure aligns with the NMR data by comparing the expected chemical shifts and splitting patterns.
